  "Solution": {
    "S": "Using Kirchhoff's voltage law from point A to point B:\n\n$$V_A - (2 \\times 2) - 3 - (2 \\times 1) = V_B$$\n\n$$V_A - 4 - 3 - 2 = V_B$$\n\n$$V_A - 9 = V_B$$\n\n$$V_A - V_B = 9 \\text{ V}$$\n\nThus the potential difference $V_A - V_B$ is 9 V, which corresponds to option C."
  },
